5 . How would you enable RDS Storage Auto Scaling
ans.	I would enable Storage Auto Scaling in Amazon RDS by modifying the database instance and setting the maximum storage threshold. 
	This allows RDS to automatically increase storage when free space becomes low.
	It helps prevent storage exhaustion during high traffic.
	
	
	
6. How would you scale reads?
ans.I would create two MySQL Read Replicas to distribute read traffic. 
The primary database handles write operations, while Read Replicas handle read queries such as reports,
 dashboards and result searches.
 This reduces CPU load on the primary database.
 
7 How does Laravel split read/write connections
ans.Laravel supports read/write database connections in its config/database.php file.
 I configure the primary database endpoint for write operations and Read Replica endpoints for read operations.
 SELECT queries go to replicas, while INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE queries go to the primary database. 
 I also enable the sticky option to avoid some read-after-write consistency issue
 
 
