9. How would you set up access for a 4-person team?
ans= I would create four IAM users and three IAM groups:
 Developers, DevOps, and Auditors. I would add two developers to the Developers group, 
 one DevOps engineer to the DevOps group, and one auditor to the Auditors group.
 I would assign permissions according to their job responsibilities.
 
10. How would you implement least-privilege permissions?
ans= I would follow the principle of least privilege by granting each user only the permissions required for their job.
 Developers would get EC2 read-only access and write access to a specific S3 bucket.
 The DevOps engineer would get permissions to manage infrastructure,
 and the auditor would get read-only access.
 
 
11. What permissions would you give the auditor?
ans= I would attach the AWS managed ReadOnlyAccess policy to the Auditors group.
 This allows the auditor to view AWS resources and configurations across services without modifying or deleting resources.
 
 12. What is an IAM Role for EC2?
ans= An IAM Role is an identity that provides temporary permissions to AWS services or applications.
 I would create an IAM role for EC2 with read-only access to a specific S3 bucket and attach it to the EC2 instance. 
 This allows the instance to access S3 without storing permanent access keys on the server.
 
 13. How does EC2 access S3 without access keys?
ans= EC2 uses an attached IAM role to obtain temporary security credentials through the Instance Metadata Service.
 AWS automatically rotates these credentials, 
 so we don't need to store access keys on the EC2 server.
 
 14.How would you verify the IAM Role?
ans = I would connect to the EC2 instance and run aws sts get-caller-identity to verify the assumed role identity. 
Then I would run aws s3 ls to confirm that the instance can read the authorized S3 bucket. 
I would also test unauthorized actions to verify that least-privilege permissions are enforced.


15.How would you enable versioning on both S3 buckets?
Ans=
I would open the S3 bucket properties,
 go to Bucket Versioning, 
 and enable versioning on both the source and destination buckets.
 Versioning keeps multiple versions of objects and helps recover files from accidental overwrites or deletions.
 
 16.What is Cross-Region Replication (CRR)?
