29 . Draw the architecture. Example: RDS binlog to Debezium to Kafka (Amazon MSK) to
the ClickHouse Kafka engine. Or use AWS DMS, or ClickPipes.

AWS Database Migration Service (DMS) can capture changes from RDS and replicate them into supported destinations.
 I would consider it if the organization wants an AWS-managed replication service and reduced connector operations.


30 . How would you monitor replication lag, and what happens if the CDC consumer is
down for 2 hours?
ans= I would implement CDC from Amazon RDS MySQL to ClickHouse using Debezium and Amazon MSK.
 In RDS, I would use a custom parameter group with binlog_format=ROW and binlog_row_image=FULL,
 enable automated backups, and configure binlog retention for at least 72 hours, preferably 7 days depending on storage and workload.
 Debezium would read the RDS binlog and publish INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE events to MSK. ClickHouse would consume these events through its Kafka Engine
 and materialized views and insert them into a ReplacingMergeTree table.
I would use the transaction ID as the stable sorting key,
 a monotonically increasing CDC version column, and a delete marker to handle updates and deletes.
 I would monitor Debezium connector health, source lag, MSK consumer lag, ClickHouse insert errors and data freshness	
	
